    "text": "\\[\nx y^{\\prime}+2 y=\\frac{1}{x^{2} \\log x}\n\\]\n\nSTANDART FORM OF THE EQUATION:\n\\[\ny^{\\prime}+\\frac{2 y}{x}=\\frac{1}{x^{3} \\log x}\n\\]\n\nTHEN, integrating factor:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{l}\nI \\cdot F=e^{\\int \\frac{2}{x} d x}=e^{2 \\log x}=x^{2} \\\\\ny \\cdot I \\cdot F=\\int x^{2} \\cdot x^{\\frac{1}{3 \\log x} d x+c} \\\\\ny x^{2}=\\int \\frac{1}{x \\log x} d x+c\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nLET \\( \\log _{x} \\) BE \" \\( m \\) \", THEN\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{l}\ny x^{2}=\\int \\frac{1}{m} \\cdot d m+c=\\log m+c \\\\\ny x^{2}=\\log (\\log x)+c\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nif \\( y(E)=0 \\), THEN\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c}\ny(e) \\cdot e^{2}=\\log _{e}(\\log e)+c \\\\\n0=\\log _{e}(1)+c \\\\\n0=0+c \\\\\nc=0, \\text { so } \\\\\ny x^{2}=\\log \\left(\\log _{x}\\right) \\\\\ny=\\frac{\\log (\\log x)}{x^{2}}\n\\end{array}\n\\]",
